**Bug found and fixed:** the SBOM step ran the bundled interpreter without `-B` and wrote `lib/python3.14/__pycache__/platform.cpython-314.pyc` into the bundle *after* signing — the final verify caught it (`a sealed resource is missing or invalid`). All bundled-interpreter calls now use `-B`, and `build_app.sh` re-verifies after the SBOM and zips last.

